 **Definition**
-Convexity Enhancement uses knowledge of convexity to increase the step size along the ray during sphere tracing. For a convex set, the line segment from the current point to the tangent plane intersection does not intersect the surface except possibly at the endpoint [S1]. This optimization hastens convergence by leveraging convexity properties, providing a faster order of convergence than standard sphere tracing [S1].
